@prefix : <http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix xml: <http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix swrl: <http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrl#> .
@prefix swrlb: <http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrlb#> .
@prefix standard-pass-ont: <http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#> .
@base <http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont> .

<http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                         owl:versionIRI <http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont/dev> ;
                                         rdfs:comment """Version history:

2025-07-04 :

- Restructuring of the Data Definition Components
    - Renaming of DataObjectDefinition to DataElementDefinition- 
    - Restructuring the SubjectDataDefinition to be a direct subclass of  DataDescribingComponent to be on the same level as PayloadDescription (could possibly also have a matching substructure that differs between physical and data content
2021-05-19 Version 1.1.0: I2PM Standardization Meeting Spring 2021

Participants:
Matthes Elstermann – Karlsruhe Institute of Technology (KIT) matthes.elstermann@kit.edu
Herbert Kindermann – Kindermann Consulting
Robert Singer – FH Joanneum Graz
Florian Krenn – Compunity, Linz, Austria
Werner Schmidt – TH Ingolstadt
Matthias Lederer – OTH Weiden
Christian Stary – Universität Linz
André Wolski – TU Darmstadt
Albert Fleischmann – Interaktiv Unternehmensberatung

Agreed on changes:
- new Class SubjectExecutionMapping
- performance improvements
- clarification regarding EndState usage in SubjectBehavior


2018-11-22 Version 1.0.0: Standardization Meeting Ingolstadt

Agreed on Version 1.0.0 from meeting:

Participants
- Werner Schmidt
- Herbert Kindermann
- Bernhard Foltin
- André Wolski
- Florian Krenn
- Albert Fleischmann
- Matthes Elstermann

2018-11-09: Elstermann (Proposal)

clarifications for Send and Receive Transition Conditions and Sending and Receiving in regards to subjects with multiple instances (Multi-Subjects)

Transition--> hasTransitionCondition--> information about sending and receiving

ReceiveTransitionCondition
   hasReceiveType
    - ReceiveTypeMultiReceiveFromAllKnown
    - ReceiveTypeMultiReceiveFromKnwon
    - ReceiveTypeStandard
	
    hasMultiReceiveLowerBound
    hasMultiReceiveUpperBound

    requiresReceptionOfMessage
    requiresMessageSentFrom

SendTransitionCondition

  hasSendType
   - SendingTypeMultiSendToAll
   - SendingTypeMultiSendToKnown
   - SendingTypeMultiSendToNew
   - SendingTypeStandard

  hasMultiSendLowerBound
  hasMultiSendUpperBound

  requiresSendingOfMessage  (SendTransition)
  requiresMessageSentTo (SendTransition)


2018-07-05: Ingolstadt Review.

- current Status after
- Participants:
 - Herbert Kindermann
 - Albert Fleischmann
 - Werner Schmidt
 - Florian Krenn
 - Florian J. Strecker
 - Matthes Elstermann"""@en ;
                                         owl:priorVersion "http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont/1.1.0" .

#################################################################
#    Datatypes
#################################################################

###  http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dayTimeDuration
xsd:dayTimeDuration rdf:type rdfs:Datatype .


###  http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#yearMonthDuration
xsd:yearMonthDuration rdf:type rdfs:Datatype .


#################################################################
#    Object Properties
#################################################################

###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#SimplePASSObjectProperty
standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                           rdfs:comment "Every element/sub-class of SimplePASSObjectProperties is also a Child of PASSModelObjectPropertiy. This is simply a surrogate class to group all simple elements together" .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#belongsTo
standard-pass-ont:belongsTo rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                            rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                               standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                            owl:inverseOf standard-pass-ont:contains ;
                            rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModelElement ;
                            rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModelElement ;
                            rdfs:comment "Generic ObjectProperty that links two process elements, where one is contained in the other (inverse of contains)."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#contains
standard-pass-ont:contains rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                           rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                              standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                           rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModelElement ;
                           rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModelElement ;
                           rdfs:comment "Generic ObjectProperty that links two model elements where one contains another (possible multiple)."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#containsBaseBehavior
standard-pass-ont:containsBaseBehavior rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                       rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:containsBehavior ;
                                       owl:inverseOf standard-pass-ont:isBaseBehaviorOf ;
                                       rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:Subject ;
                                       rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:SubjectBaseBehavior .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#containsBehavior
standard-pass-ont:containsBehavior rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:contains ;
                                   rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:Subject ;
                                   rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:SubjectBehavior .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#containsPayloadDescription
standard-pass-ont:containsPayloadDescription rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                             rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:contains ;
                                             rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:MessageSpecification ;
                                             rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:PayloadDescription .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#guardedBy
standard-pass-ont:guardedBy rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                            rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                            owl:inverseOf standard-pass-ont:guardsState ;
                            rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          owl:unionOf ( standard-pass-ont:Action
                                                        standard-pass-ont:State
                                                      )
                                        ] ;
                            rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:GuardBehavior .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#guardsBehavior
standard-pass-ont:guardsBehavior rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                 rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                 rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:GuardBehavior ;
                                 rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:SubjectBehavior ;
                                 rdfs:comment "Links a GuardBehavior to another SubjectBehavior. Automatically all individual states in the guarded behavior are guarded by the guard behavior. There is an SWRL Rule in the ontology for that purpose."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#guardsState
standard-pass-ont:guardsState rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                              rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                              rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:GuardBehavior ;
                              rdfs:range [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                           owl:unionOf ( standard-pass-ont:Action
                                                         standard-pass-ont:State
                                                       )
                                         ] .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasAdditionalAttribute
standard-pass-ont:hasAdditionalAttribute rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                         rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModelElement ;
                                         rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:AdditionalAttribute .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasCorrespondent
standard-pass-ont:hasCorrespondent rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                      standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                   owl:inverseOf standard-pass-ont:hasMessageExchange ;
                                   rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:Subject ;
                                   rdfs:comment "Generic super class for the ObjectProperties that link a Subject with a MessageExchange either in the role of Sender or Receiver."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasDataDefinition
standard-pass-ont:hasDataDefinition rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                    rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                       standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                    rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:DataElementDefinition .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasDataMappingFunction
standard-pass-ont:hasDataMappingFunction rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                            standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                         rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                       owl:unionOf ( standard-pass-ont:ReceiveTransition
                                                                     standard-pass-ont:SendTransition
                                                                     standard-pass-ont:State
                                                                   )
                                                     ] ;
                                         rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:DataMappingFunction .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasDataType
standard-pass-ont:hasDataType rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                              rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                 standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                              rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                            owl:unionOf ( standard-pass-ont:DataElementDefinition
                                                          standard-pass-ont:PayloadDescription
                                                        )
                                          ] ;
                              rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:DataTypeDefinition .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasEndState
standard-pass-ont:hasEndState rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                              rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                 standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                              owl:inverseOf standard-pass-ont:isEndStateOf ;
                              rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                            owl:unionOf ( standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegmentPath
                                                          standard-pass-ont:SubjectBehavior
                                                        )
                                          ] ;
                              rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:State ,
                                         [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                           owl:complementOf standard-pass-ont:SendState
                                         ] .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasFunctionSpecification
standard-pass-ont:hasFunctionSpecification rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                           rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                              standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                           rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:State ;
                                           rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:FunctionSpecification .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasHandlingStrategy
standard-pass-ont:hasHandlingStrategy rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                      rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                      rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:InputPoolConstraint ;
                                      rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:InputPoolContstraintHandlingStrategy .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasIncomingMessageExchange
standard-pass-ont:hasIncomingMessageExchange rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                             rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasMessageExchange ;
                                             owl:inverseOf standard-pass-ont:hasReceiver ;
                                             rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:Subject ;
                                             rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:MessageExchange .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasIncomingTransition
standard-pass-ont:hasIncomingTransition rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                        rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                           standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                        owl:inverseOf standard-pass-ont:hasTargetState ;
                                        rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:State ;
                                        rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:Transition .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasInitialState
standard-pass-ont:hasInitialState rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                  rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                     standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                  owl:inverseOf standard-pass-ont:isInitialStateOf ;
                                  rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                owl:unionOf ( standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegmentPath
                                                              standard-pass-ont:SubjectBehavior
                                                            )
                                              ] ;
                                  rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:State .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasInputPoolConstraint
standard-pass-ont:hasInputPoolConstraint rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                         rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:Subject ;
                                         rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:InputPoolConstraint .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasKeyValuePair
standard-pass-ont:hasKeyValuePair rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasMessageExchange
standard-pass-ont:hasMessageExchange rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                     rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                        standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                     rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:Subject ;
                                     rdfs:comment "Generic super class for the ObjectProperties linking a subject with either incoming or outgoing MessageExchanges."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasMessageType
standard-pass-ont:hasMessageType rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                 rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                    standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                 rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                               owl:unionOf ( standard-pass-ont:MessageExchange
                                                             standard-pass-ont:MessageSenderTypeConstraint
                                                             standard-pass-ont:MessageTypeConstraint
                                                           )
                                             ] ;
                                 rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:MessageSpecification ;
                                 rdfs:comment "MessageExchanges as well as InputPool constraints regarding messages should be linked to certain types of messages that have been defined in this or another model."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasOutgoingMessageExchange
standard-pass-ont:hasOutgoingMessageExchange rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                             rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasMessageExchange ;
                                             owl:inverseOf standard-pass-ont:hasSender ;
                                             rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:Subject ;
                                             rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:MessageExchange .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasOutgoingTransition
standard-pass-ont:hasOutgoingTransition rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                        rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                           standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                        owl:inverseOf standard-pass-ont:hasSourceState ;
                                        rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:State ;
                                        rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:Transition .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasReceiveType
standard-pass-ont:hasReceiveType rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                 rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                 rdfs:comment """In simple processes every ReceiveTransitionCondition will have the standard Receive type.

However, in processes  where subjects can be instantiated multiple times (Multi-Subjects), the receive type will define whether the reception of a message will require answers from one, multiple, are all known existing instances of the corresponding subject."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasReceiver
standard-pass-ont:hasReceiver rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                              rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasCorrespondent ;
                              rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:MessageExchange ;
                              rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:Subject .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasRelationToModelComponent
standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                              rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModelElement ;
                                              rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModelElement ;
                                              rdfs:comment "Generic super class of all object properties in the standard-pass-ont that are used to link model elements with one-another."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasSendType
standard-pass-ont:hasSendType rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                              rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                              rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:SendTransitionCondition ;
                              rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:SendType ;
                              rdfs:comment """In simple processes every sendtransitionCondition will have the standard Send type.

However, in Process with where subjects can be instantiated multiple times (Multi-Subjects), the send type will define whether the sending of a message will create a new subject-instance, or if the send message should be send to one, multiple, are all existing instances."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasSender
standard-pass-ont:hasSender rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                            rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasCorrespondent ;
                            rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:MessageExchange ;
                            rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:Subject .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasSourceState
standard-pass-ont:hasSourceState rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                 rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                    standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                 rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:Transition ;
                                 rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:State .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasStartSubject
standard-pass-ont:hasStartSubject rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                  rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                     standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                  rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModel ;
                                  rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:StartSubject .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasSubjectExecutionMapping
standard-pass-ont:hasSubjectExecutionMapping rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                             rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                             rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:Subject ;
                                             rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:SubjectExecutionMapping .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasTargetState
standard-pass-ont:hasTargetState rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                 rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                    standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                 rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:Transition ;
                                 rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:State .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasTransitionCondition
standard-pass-ont:hasTransitionCondition rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                            standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                         rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:Transition ;
                                         rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:TransitionCondition .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#isBaseBehaviorOf
standard-pass-ont:isBaseBehaviorOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:belongsTo ;
                                   rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:SubjectBaseBehavior ;
                                   rdfs:comment "A specialized version of the \"belongsTo\" ObjectProperty to denote that a -SubjectBehavior belongs to a Subject as its BaseBehavior"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#isEndStateOf
standard-pass-ont:isEndStateOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                               rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                  standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                               rdfs:domain [ owl:intersectionOf ( standard-pass-ont:State
                                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                    owl:complementOf standard-pass-ont:SendState
                                                                  ]
                                                                ) ;
                                             rdf:type owl:Class
                                           ] ;
                               rdfs:range [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                            owl:unionOf ( standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegmentPath
                                                          standard-pass-ont:SubjectBehavior
                                                        )
                                          ] .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#isInitialStateOf
standard-pass-ont:isInitialStateOf rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                      standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                   rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:State ;
                                   rdfs:range [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                owl:unionOf ( standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegmentPath
                                                              standard-pass-ont:SubjectBehavior
                                                            )
                                              ] .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#isReferencedBy
standard-pass-ont:isReferencedBy rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                 rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                 owl:inverseOf standard-pass-ont:references .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#references
standard-pass-ont:references rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                             rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                             rdfs:comment """Very generic object property.

Describes that the element this property originates from, references another model element possibly in another model.

E.g. an interface subject references another process-model.

A StateReference may reference a state in another Behavior

Or an InputPool constraint references a Subject and/or a message."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#referencesMacroBehavior
standard-pass-ont:referencesMacroBehavior rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                          rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:references ;
                                          rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:MacroState ;
                                          rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:MacroBehavior ;
                                          rdfs:comment "Macro States reference Macro Behaviors"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#requiresMessageSentFrom
standard-pass-ont:requiresMessageSentFrom rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                          rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                             standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                          rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:ReceiveTransitionCondition ;
                                          rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:Subject ;
                                          rdfs:comment """This ObjectProperty links a ReceiveTransitionCondition with an according sender subject.

The same information is part of the \"requiresPerformedMessageExchange\"-Object property that is only existent if the TransitionCondition is fully specified."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#requiresMessageSentTo
standard-pass-ont:requiresMessageSentTo rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                        rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                           standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                        rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:SendTransitionCondition ;
                                        rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:Subject ;
                                        rdfs:comment """This ObjectProperty links a SendTransitionCondition with an according sender subject.

The same information is part of the \"requiresPerformedMessageExchange\"-Object property that is only existent if the TransitionCondition is fully specified."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#requiresPerformedMessageExchange
standard-pass-ont:requiresPerformedMessageExchange rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                                      standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                                   rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:MessageExchangeCondition ;
                                                   rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:MessageExchange ;
                                                   rdfs:comment """This DataProperty links a send or receive transition condition to a specific message exchange.

For send transition it implies that the according message has been send to the in-box of the corresponding receiver subject.

For receive transitions it implies that the according message from the corresponding sender subject is in the in-box and could be extracted.

When a MessageExchangeCondition is not fully specified (missing sender, receiver, or message) it cannot reference a specific message exchange.

In that case the individual reference must contain the according information:

requiresSendingOfMessage  (SendTransition)
requiresMessageSentTo (SendTransition)
requiresReceptionOfMessage (ReceiveTransition)
requiresMessageSentFrom (ReceiveTransition)"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#requiresReceptionOfMessage
standard-pass-ont:requiresReceptionOfMessage rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                             rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                                standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                             rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:ReceiveTransitionCondition ;
                                             rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:MessageSpecification ;
                                             rdfs:comment """This ObjectProperty links a ReceiveTransitionCondition with an according MessageSpecification

The same information is part of the \"requiresPerformedMessageExchange\"-Object property that is only existent if the TransitionCondition is fully specified."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#requiresSendingOfMessage
standard-pass-ont:requiresSendingOfMessage rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                           rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSObjectProperty ,
                                                              standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                           rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:SendTransitionCondition ;
                                           rdfs:range standard-pass-ont:MessageSpecification ;
                                           rdfs:comment """This ObjectProperty links a SendTransitionCondition with an according MessageSpecification

The same information is part of the \"requiresPerformedMessageExchange\"-Object property that is only existent if the TransitionCondition is fully specified."""@en .


#################################################################
#    Data properties
#################################################################

###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#PASSModelDataProperty
standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                        rdfs:subPropertyOf owl:topDataProperty ;
                                        rdfs:comment "Generic super class of all DataProperties that PASS process model elements may have."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#SimplePASSDataProperties
standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSDataProperties rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                           rdfs:comment "Every element/sub-class of SimplePASSDataProperties is also a Child of PASSModelDataPropertiy. This is simply a surrogate class to group all simple elements together"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasBusinessDayDurationTimeOutTime
standard-pass-ont:hasBusinessDayDurationTimeOutTime rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                                    rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasDurationTimeOutTime ;
                                                    rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:BusinessDayTimerTransitionCondition ;
                                                    rdfs:range xsd:dayTimeDuration .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasCalendarBasedFrequencyOrDate
standard-pass-ont:hasCalendarBasedFrequencyOrDate rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                                  rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasReoccuranceFrequenyOrDate ;
                                                  rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:CalendarBasedReminderTransitionCondition .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasDataMappingString
standard-pass-ont:hasDataMappingString rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                       rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ,
                                                          standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSDataProperties .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasDayTimeDurationTimeOutTime
standard-pass-ont:hasDayTimeDurationTimeOutTime rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                                rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasDurationTimeOutTime ;
                                                rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:DayTimeTimerTransitionCondition ;
                                                rdfs:range xsd:dayTimeDuration .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasDurationTimeOutTime
standard-pass-ont:hasDurationTimeOutTime rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasTimeValue ;
                                         rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:TimerTransitionCondition .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasExecutionMappingDefinition
standard-pass-ont:hasExecutionMappingDefinition rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                                rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ;
                                                rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                              owl:unionOf ( standard-pass-ont:Subject
                                                                            standard-pass-ont:SubjectExecutionMapping
                                                                          )
                                                            ] ;
                                                rdfs:range xsd:string .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasFeelExpressionAsDataMapping
standard-pass-ont:hasFeelExpressionAsDataMapping rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                                 rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ;
                                                 rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:DataMappingFunction ;
                                                 rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                                                 rdfs:comment """See https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN for specification of Feel-Statement-Strings

The idea of these expression is to map data fields from and to the internal Data storage of a subject"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasGraphicalRepresentation
standard-pass-ont:hasGraphicalRepresentation rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                             rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ;
                                             rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModelElement ;
                                             rdfs:comment """The process models are in principle abstract graph structures. Yet the visualization of process models is very important since many process models are initially created in a graphical form using a graphical graph editor (e.g. MS Visio, yEd, etc.) that was created to foster human comprehensibility. 

If available any process element may have a graphical representation attached to it.
"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasKey
standard-pass-ont:hasKey rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                         rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ,
                                            standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSDataProperties ;
                         rdfs:range xsd:string .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasLimit
standard-pass-ont:hasLimit rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                           rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ;
                           rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:InputPoolConstraint ;
                           rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasMaximumSubjectInstanceRestriction
standard-pass-ont:hasMaximumSubjectInstanceRestriction rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                                       rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ,
                                                                          standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSDataProperties ;
                                                       rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:Subject ;
                                                       rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasMetaData
standard-pass-ont:hasMetaData rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                              rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ;
                              rdfs:range xsd:string .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasModelComponentComment
standard-pass-ont:hasModelComponentComment rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                           rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ,
                                                              standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSDataProperties ;
                                           rdfs:comment "equivalent to rdfs:comment"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasModelComponentID
standard-pass-ont:hasModelComponentID rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                      rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ,
                                                         standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSDataProperties ;
                                      rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModelElement ;
                                      rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                                      rdfs:comment "The unique ID of a PASSProcessModelComponent"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasModelComponentLabel
standard-pass-ont:hasModelComponentLabel rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ,
                                                            standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSDataProperties ;
                                         rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModelElement ;
                                         rdfs:comment "The human legible label or description of a model element."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasMultiReceiveLowerBound
standard-pass-ont:hasMultiReceiveLowerBound rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ;
                                            rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:ReceiveTransitionCondition ;
                                            rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasMultiReceiveUpperBound
standard-pass-ont:hasMultiReceiveUpperBound rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ;
                                            rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:ReceiveTransitionCondition ;
                                            rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasMultiSendLowerBound
standard-pass-ont:hasMultiSendLowerBound rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ;
                                         rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:SendTransitionCondition ;
                                         rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasMultiSendUpperBound
standard-pass-ont:hasMultiSendUpperBound rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ;
                                         rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:SendTransitionCondition ;
                                         rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasPriorityNumber
standard-pass-ont:hasPriorityNumber rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                    rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ,
                                                       standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSDataProperties ;
                                    rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger ;
                                    rdfs:comment """Transitions or Behaviors have numbers that denote their execution priority in situations where two or more options could be executed.

This is important for automated execution.

E.g. when two messages are in the in-box and could be followed, the message denoted on the transition with the higher priority (lower priority number) is taken out and processed.

Similarly, SubjectBehaviors with higher priority (lower priority number) are to be executed before Behaviors with lower priority."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasReoccuranceFrequenyOrDate
standard-pass-ont:hasReoccuranceFrequenyOrDate rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                               rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasTimeValue ;
                                               rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:ReminderEventTransitionCondition ;
                                               rdfs:comment """A data field meant for the two classes ReoccuranceTimeOutTransition and ReoccuranceTimeOutExitCondition.

ToDo: Define the according data format for describing the iteration frequencies or reoccurring dates. Opinion: rather complex: expressive capabilities should cover expressions like: \"every 2nd Monday of Month at 7:30 in Morning.\" Every 29th of July\" or \"Every Hour\", \"ever 25 Minuets\" , \"once each day\", \"twice each week\" etc."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasSVGRepresentation
standard-pass-ont:hasSVGRepresentation rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                       rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasGraphicalRepresentation ;
                                       rdfs:range rdf:XMLLiteral ;
                                       rdfs:comment """The Scalable Vector Graphic (SVG) XML format is a text based standard to describe vector graphics. 

Adding according image information as XML literals is therefor a suitable, yet not necessarily easily changeable option to include the graphical representation of model elements in the an OWL file."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasTimeBasedReoccuranceFrequencyOrDate
standard-pass-ont:hasTimeBasedReoccuranceFrequencyOrDate rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasReoccuranceFrequenyOrDate ;
                                                         rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:TimeBasedReminderTransitionCondition .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasTimeValue
standard-pass-ont:hasTimeValue rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                               rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ;
                               rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             owl:unionOf ( standard-pass-ont:TimeTransitionCondition
                                                           standard-pass-ont:TimerTransition
                                                         )
                                           ] ;
                               rdfs:comment "Generic super class for all data properties of time based transitions."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasToolSpecificDefinition
standard-pass-ont:hasToolSpecificDefinition rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ;
                                            rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModelElement ;
                                            rdfs:comment """This is a placeholder DataProperty meant as a tie in point for tool vendors to include tool specific data values/properties into models. 

By denoting their own data properties as sub-classes to this one the according data fields can easily be recognized as such. However, this is only an option and a place holder to remind that something like this is possible."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasValue
standard-pass-ont:hasValue rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                           rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ,
                                              standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSDataProperties .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#hasYearMonthDurationTimeOutTime
standard-pass-ont:hasYearMonthDurationTimeOutTime rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                                  rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:hasDurationTimeOutTime ;
                                                  rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:YearMonthTimerTransitionCondition ;
                                                  rdfs:range xsd:yearMonthDuration .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#isOptionalToEndChoiceSegmentPath
standard-pass-ont:isOptionalToEndChoiceSegmentPath rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ;
                                                   rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegmentPath ;
                                                   rdfs:range xsd:boolean .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#isOptionalToStartChoiceSegmentPath
standard-pass-ont:isOptionalToStartChoiceSegmentPath rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
                                                     rdfs:subPropertyOf standard-pass-ont:PASSModelDataProperty ;
                                                     rdfs:domain standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegmentPath ;
                                                     rdfs:range xsd:boolean .


#################################################################
#    Classes
#################################################################

###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#Action
standard-pass-ont:Action rdf:type owl:Class ;
                         rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:BehaviorDescribingComponent ,
                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                           owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:contains ;
                                           owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:Transition
                                         ] ,
                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                           owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:contains ;
                                           owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                           owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:State
                                         ] ;
                         rdfs:comment "An Action is a grouping concept that groups a state with all its outgoing valid transitions."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#AdditionalAttribute
standard-pass-ont:AdditionalAttribute rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                      rdfs:subClassOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasKeyValuePair ;
                                                        owl:minQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                        owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:KeyValuePair
                                                      ] .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#BehaviorDescribingComponent
standard-pass-ont:BehaviorDescribingComponent rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModelElement ,
                                                              [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:belongsTo ;
                                                                owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                                owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:SubjectBehavior
                                                              ] ;
                                              rdfs:comment "Group of PASS-Model components that describe aspects of the behavior of subjects"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#BusinessDayTimerTransition
standard-pass-ont:BusinessDayTimerTransition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:TimerTransition ;
                                             rdfs:comment """Timer transitions, denote time outs for the state they originate from.  The condition for a timer transition is that a certain amount of time has passed since the state it originates from has been entered.

The time unit for this timer transition is measured in business days. The definition of a business day depends on a subject's relevant or legal location."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#BusinessDayTimerTransitionCondition
standard-pass-ont:BusinessDayTimerTransitionCondition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                      rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:TimerTransitionCondition ;
                                                      rdfs:comment "Transition Condition for the according BusinessDayTimerTransition. Same as the DayTimeDurationExpiredTimerTransitionCondition, but with Business Days as the time measuring unit (requires a location reference)"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#CalendarBasedReminderTransition
standard-pass-ont:CalendarBasedReminderTransition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                  rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:ReminderTransition ;
                                                  owl:disjointWith standard-pass-ont:TimeBasedReminderTransition ;
                                                  rdfs:comment """A reminder transition, for defining exit conditions for states measured in calendar years or months
		
		Conditions are e.g.: reaching of (in model) preset calendar date (e.g. 1st of July) or the reoccurrence  of a a long running frequency (\"every Month\", \"2 times a year\")"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#CalendarBasedReminderTransitionCondition
standard-pass-ont:CalendarBasedReminderTransitionCondition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                           rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:ReminderEventTransitionCondition ;
                                                           owl:disjointWith standard-pass-ont:TimeBasedReminderTransitionCondition ;
                                                           rdfs:comment """The according TransitionCondition type for the CalendarBasedReminderTransition.
		
		e.g. reaching of (in model) preset calendar date (e.g. 1st of July) or the reoccurrence  of a a long running frequency (\"every Month\", \"2 times a year\")"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#ChoiceSegment
standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegment rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:State ,
                                                [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                  owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:contains ;
                                                  owl:minQualifiedCardinality "2"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                  owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegmentPath
                                                ] ;
                                rdfs:comment "ChoiceSegments are groups of defined ChoiceSegementPaths. The paths may contain any amount of states. However, those states may not reach out of the bounds of the ChoiceSegmentPath."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#ChoiceSegmentPath
standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegmentPath rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                    rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:State ,
                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                      owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:contains ;
                                                      owl:minQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                      owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:State
                                                    ] ,
                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                      owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:belongsTo ;
                                                      owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                      owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegment
                                                    ] ,
                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                      owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasEndState ;
                                                      owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                      owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:State
                                                    ] ,
                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                      owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasInitialState ;
                                                      owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                      owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:InitialStateOfChoiceSegmentPath
                                                    ] ,
                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                      owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:isOptionalToEndChoiceSegmentPath ;
                                                      owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                      owl:onDataRange xsd:boolean
                                                    ] ,
                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                      owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:isOptionalToStartChoiceSegmentPath ;
                                                      owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                      owl:onDataRange xsd:boolean
                                                    ] ;
                                    rdfs:comment """ChoiceSegments are groups of defined ChoiceSegementPaths. The paths may contain any amount of states. However, those states may not reach out of the bounds of the ChoiceSegmentPath.

The path may contain any amount of states but may those states may not reach out of the bounds of the choice segment path.

Similar to an initial state of a behavior a choice segment path must have one determined initial state.

A transition within a choice segment path must not have a target state that is not inside the same choice segment path."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#CommunicationAct
standard-pass-ont:CommunicationAct rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                   rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:FunctionSpecification ;
                                   owl:disjointWith standard-pass-ont:DoFunction ;
                                   rdfs:comment "A super class for specialized FunctionSpecification of communication acts (send and receive)"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#CommunicationTransition
standard-pass-ont:CommunicationTransition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSElement ,
                                                          standard-pass-ont:Transition ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasTransitionCondition ;
                                                            owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                            owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:MessageExchangeCondition
                                                          ] ;
                                          rdfs:comment "A super class for the CommunicationTransitions."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#CustomOrExternalDataTypeDefinition
standard-pass-ont:CustomOrExternalDataTypeDefinition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                     rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:DataTypeDefinition ;
                                                     rdfs:comment "Using this class, tool vendors can include their own custom data definitions in the model."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DataDescribingComponent
standard-pass-ont:DataDescribingComponent rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModelElement ;
                                          rdfs:comment """Subject-Oriented PASS Process Models are in general about describing the activities and interaction of active entities. Yet these interactions are rarely done without data that is being generated by activities and transported via messages. While not considered by Börger's PASS interpreter, the community agreed on adding the ability to integrate the means to describe data objects or data structures to the model and enabling their connection to the process model. 

It may be defined that messages or subject have their individual $DataObjectDefinition$ in form of a $SubjectDataDefinition$ in the case of $FullySpecifiedSubject$s and  $PayloadDataObjectDesfinition$ in the case of $MessageSpecifications$

In general, it expected that these $DataObjectDefinition$ list on or more data fields for the message or subject with an internal data type that is described via a $DataTypeDefinition$.

There is a rudimentary concept for a simple build-in data type definition closely oriented at the concept of ActNConnect. Otherwise, the principle idea of the OWL standard is to allow and employ existing or custom technologies for the serialized definition of data structures ($CustomOrExternalDataTypeDefinition$) such as XML-Schemata (XSD), according elements with JSON or directly the powerful expressiveness of OWL itself."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DataElementDefinition
standard-pass-ont:DataElementDefinition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:DataDescribingComponent ,
                                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                          owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasDataType ;
                                                          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                          owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:DataTypeDefinition
                                                        ] ;
                                        rdfs:comment """Data Element Definitions are model elements used to describe that certain other model elements (mainly Payload Data Definitions and Subject Data Definitions) may posses or carrier data.

E.G. a message may carrier/include a Business Objects. Or the private Data Space of a Subject may contain several Data Objects. 

A Data element should refer to a DataTypeDefinition denoting its DataType and structure. 

DataElements: states that a data item does exist (similar to a variable in programming)
DataType: the definition of an Data Object's structure."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DataMappingFunction
standard-pass-ont:DataMappingFunction rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                      rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:DataDescribingComponent ,
                                                      standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSElement ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        owl:unionOf ( [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                        owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasFeelExpressionAsDataMapping ;
                                                                        owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                                        owl:onDataRange xsd:string
                                                                      ]
                                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                        owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasToolSpecificDefinition ;
                                                                        owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                                        owl:onDataRange xsd:string
                                                                      ]
                                                                    )
                                                      ] ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasDataMappingString ;
                                                        owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                        owl:onDataRange xsd:string
                                                      ] ;
                                      rdfs:comment """ToDo: Standard Format for DataMappingFunctions must be define: (Options: XML,OWL,JSON)
		
		Definitions of the ability/need to write or read data to and from a subject's personal data storage.

DataMappingFunctions are behavior describing components since they define what the subject is supposed to do (mapping and translating data)

Mapping may be done during reception of message, where data is taken from the message/Business Object (BO) and mapped/put into the local data field. 

It may be done during sending of a message where data is taken from the local vault and put into a BO.

Or it may occur during executing a do function, where it is used to define read(get) and write (set) functions for the local data."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DataMappingIncomingToLocal
standard-pass-ont:DataMappingIncomingToLocal rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:DataMappingFunction ;
                                             owl:disjointWith standard-pass-ont:DataMappingLocalToOutgoing ;
                                             rdfs:comment "A DataMapping that specifies how data is mapped from an an external source (message, function call etc.) to a subject's private defined data space."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DataMappingLocalToOutgoing
standard-pass-ont:DataMappingLocalToOutgoing rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:DataMappingFunction ;
                                             rdfs:comment "A DataMapping that specifies how data is mapped from a subject's private data space to an an external destination (message, function call etc.)"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DataObjectListDefintion
standard-pass-ont:DataObjectListDefintion rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:DataElementDefinition ;
                                          rdfs:comment """Data definition concept for PASS model build in capabilities of data modeling. Defines a simple list structure.
		"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DataTypeDefinition
standard-pass-ont:DataTypeDefinition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                     rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:DataDescribingComponent ,
                                                     [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                       owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:contains ;
                                                       owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:DataElementDefinition
                                                     ] ;
                                     rdfs:comment """

Data Type Definitions are complex descriptions of the supposed structure of Data Objects.

DataObject: states that a data item does exist (similar to a variable in programming)
DataType: the definition of an Data Object's structure."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DayTimeTimerTransition
standard-pass-ont:DayTimeTimerTransition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                         rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:TimerTransition ;
                                         rdfs:comment """Timer Transitions, denoting time outs for the state they originate from.  The condition for a timer transition is that a certain amount of time has passed since the state it originates from has been entered.

Day or Time Timers are measured in normal 24 hour days. Following the XML standard for time and day duration. They are to be differed from the timers that are timeout in units of years or months."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DayTimeTimerTransitionCondition
standard-pass-ont:DayTimeTimerTransitionCondition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                  rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:TimerTransitionCondition ,
                                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                    owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasTimeValue ;
                                                                    owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                                    owl:onDataRange xsd:dateTime
                                                                  ] ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "A Timer Transition Condition that is fulfilled if a certain time defined in Days or hours, minuets, seconds or fractions of seconds, has passed since the state this condition belongs to has been entered."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DoFunction
standard-pass-ont:DoFunction rdf:type owl:Class ;
                             rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:FunctionSpecification ;
                             rdfs:comment """Specifications or descriptions for Do-Functions describe in detail what the subject carrier is supposed to do in an according state.

The default DoFunction 1: present the surrounding execution environment with the given exit choices/conditions and receive choice of one exit option --> define its Condition to be fulfilled in order to go to the next according state. 

The default DoFunction 2: execute automatic rule evaluation (see DoTransitionCondition)

More specialized Do-Function Specifications may contain Data mappings denoting what of a subjects internal local Data can and should be:

a) read: in order to simply see it or in order to send it of to an external function (e.g. a web service)

b) write: in order to write incoming Data from e.g. a web Service or user input, to the local data fault

"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DoState
standard-pass-ont:DoState rdf:type owl:Class ;
                          rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:StandardPASSState ,
                                          [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                            owl:complementOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasOutgoingTransition ;
                                                               owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:ReceiveTransition
                                                             ]
                                          ] ,
                                          [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                            owl:complementOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasOutgoingTransition ;
                                                               owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:SendTransition
                                                             ]
                                          ] ,
                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasDataMappingFunction ;
                                            owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:DataMappingIncomingToLocal
                                          ] ,
                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasDataMappingFunction ;
                                            owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:DataMappingLocalToOutgoing
                                          ] ,
                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasFunctionSpecification ;
                                            owl:allValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:DoFunction
                                          ] ;
                          owl:disjointWith standard-pass-ont:ReceiveState ,
                                           standard-pass-ont:SendState ;
                          rdfs:comment "The standard state in a PASS subject behavior diagram denoting an action or activity of the subject in itself."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DoTransition
standard-pass-ont:DoTransition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                               rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSElement ,
                                               standard-pass-ont:Transition ,
                                               [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                 owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasPriorityNumber ;
                                                 owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                 owl:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                               ] .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DoTransitionCondition
standard-pass-ont:DoTransitionCondition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSElement ,
                                                        standard-pass-ont:TransitionCondition ;
                                        rdfs:comment """A TransitionCondition for the according DoTransitions and DoStates. 
		"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DynamicSubjectExecutionMapping
standard-pass-ont:DynamicSubjectExecutionMapping rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                 rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:SubjectExecutionMapping ;
                                                 owl:disjointWith standard-pass-ont:StaticSubjectExecutionMapping ;
                                                 rdfs:comment """In an organisation with multiple hierarchical tiers, an agent \"Marry\" could be the supervisor for \"Paul\" and be able to authorize his vacations, while having to request her vacations in principle form \"Mark\", who is her supervisor.

Ideally, whenever some agent/subject-carrier initiates the vacation request process as an employee, the Subject \"Supervising Manager\" should automatically be mapped to her or his specific current supervisor.

Furthermore, if that specific agent is not available but there are rules to determine a deputy or substitute, the subject should automatically be be mapped to that substitute. E.g. if \"Paul\" wants his vacation to be authorized, but \"Marry\" is currently on vacation herself, someone else should be there to fill in the role of \"Supervising Manager\", namely \"Mark\" as her supervisor.

Such logic / rules can be stored in a DynamicSubjectExecutionMapping object."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#EndState
standard-pass-ont:EndState rdf:type owl:Class ;
                           rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSElement ,
                                           standard-pass-ont:State ;
                           owl:disjointWith standard-pass-ont:SendState ;
                           rdfs:comment """An end state a behavior. A subject behavior may have one or more end states. Only Do and Receive states may be end states. Send States cannot be end states.

There are no individual end states that are not Do, Send, or Receive States at the same time."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#FullySpecifiedSubject
standard-pass-ont:FullySpecifiedSubject rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:Subject ,
                                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                          owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasInputPoolConstraint ;
                                                          owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:InputPoolConstraint
                                                        ] ,
                                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                          owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:containsBehavior ;
                                                          owl:minQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                          owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:SubjectBehavior
                                                        ] ,
                                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                          owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:containsBaseBehavior ;
                                                          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                          owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:SubjectBehavior
                                                        ] ,
                                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                          owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasDataDefinition ;
                                                          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                          owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:SubjectDataDefinition
                                                        ] ;
                                        owl:disjointWith standard-pass-ont:InterfaceSubject ;
                                        rdfs:comment "Fully specified Subjects in a PASS graph are entities that, in contrast to interface subjects, linked to one ore more Behaviors (they posses a behavior)."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#FunctionSpecification
standard-pass-ont:FunctionSpecification rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:BehaviorDescribingComponent ,
                                                        standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSElement ,
                                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                          owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasToolSpecificDefinition ;
                                                          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                          owl:onDataRange xsd:string
                                                        ] ;
                                        rdfs:comment """

A function specification for state denotes

Concept: Definitions of calls of (mostly technical) functions  (e.g. Web-service, Scripts, Database access,) that are not part of the process model

Function Specifications are more than \"Data Properties\"? --> - If special function types (e.g. Defaults) are supposed to be reused, having them as explicit entities is a the better OWL-modeling choice.

"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#GenericReturnToOriginReference
standard-pass-ont:GenericReturnToOriginReference rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                 rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:State .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#GuardBehavior
standard-pass-ont:GuardBehavior rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:SubjectBehavior ,
                                                [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                  owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:guardsBehavior ;
                                                  owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:SubjectBehavior
                                                ] ,
                                                [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                  owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:guardsState ;
                                                  owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:State
                                                ] ;
                                rdfs:comment """A guard behavior is a special usually additional behavior that guards the Base Behavior of a subject.

It starts with a (guard) receive state denoting a special interrupting message.  Upon reception of that message the subject will execute the according receive transition and the follow up states until it is either redirected to a state on the base behavior or terminates in an end-state within the guard behavior.
"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#InitialStateOfBehavior
standard-pass-ont:InitialStateOfBehavior rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                         rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSElement ,
                                                         standard-pass-ont:State ;
                                         rdfs:comment "The initial state of a behavior"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#InitialStateOfChoiceSegmentPath
standard-pass-ont:InitialStateOfChoiceSegmentPath rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                  rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:State ,
                                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                    owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:belongsTo ;
                                                                    owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                                    owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegmentPath
                                                                  ] ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "Similar to an initial state of a behavior a choice segment path must have one determined initial state"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#InputPoolConstraint
standard-pass-ont:InputPoolConstraint rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                      rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:InteractionDescribingComponent ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasHandlingStrategy ;
                                                        owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                        owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:InputPoolContstraintHandlingStrategy
                                                      ] ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasLimit ;
                                                        owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                        owl:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                      ] ;
                                      rdfs:comment """Subjects do implicitly posses input pools.

During automatic execution of a PASS model in a work-flow engine this message box is filled with messages.

Without any constraints models this message in-box is assumed to be able to store an infinite amount of messages. 

For some modeling concepts though it may be of importance to restrict the size of the input pool for certain messages or senders. 

This is done using several different Type of InputPoolConstraints that are attached to a fully specified subject.

Should a constraint be applicable, an \"InputPoolConstraintHandlingStrategy\" will be executed by a work-flow engine to determine what to do with the message that does not fit in the pool.

Limiting the input pool for certain reasons to size 0 together with the InputPoolConstraintStrategy-Blocking is effectively modeling that a communication must happen synchronously instead of the standard asynchronous mode. The sender can send his message only if the receiver is in an according receive state, so the message can be handled directly without being stored in the in-box."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#InputPoolContstraintHandlingStrategy
standard-pass-ont:InputPoolContstraintHandlingStrategy rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                       owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                             owl:oneOf ( standard-pass-ont:InputPoolConstraintStrategy-Blocking
                                                                                         standard-pass-ont:InputPoolConstraintStrategy-DeleteLatest
                                                                                         standard-pass-ont:InputPoolConstraintStrategy-DeleteOldest
                                                                                         standard-pass-ont:InputPoolConstraintStrategy-Drop
                                                                                       )
                                                                           ] ;
                                                       rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:InteractionDescribingComponent ;
                                                       rdfs:comment """Should an InputPoolConstraint be applicable, an \"InputPoolConstraintHandlingStrategy\" will be executed by a work-flow engine to determine what to do with the message that does not fit in the pool.

There are    types of HandlingStrategies

InputPoolConstraintStrategy-Blocking - No new message will be adding will need to be repeated until successful

InputPoolConstraintStrategy-DeleteLatest - The new message will be added, but the last message to arrive before that applicable to the same constraint will be overwritten with the new one. (LIFO deleting concept)

InputPoolConstraintStrategy-DeleteOldest - The message will be added, but the earliest message in the input pool applicable to the same constraint will be deleted (FIFO deleting concept) 

InputPoolConstraintStrategy-Drop - Sending of the message succeeds. However the new message will not be added to the in-box. Rather it will be deleted directly."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#InteractionDescribingComponent
standard-pass-ont:InteractionDescribingComponent rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                 rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModelElement ;
                                                 rdfs:comment "This class is the super class of all model elements used to define or specify the interaction means within a process model"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#InterfaceSubject
standard-pass-ont:InterfaceSubject rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                   rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:Subject ,
                                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                     owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:containsBehavior ;
                                                     owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                     owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:SubjectBehavior
                                                   ] ,
                                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                     owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:references ;
                                                     owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                     owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:FullySpecifiedSubject
                                                   ] ;
                                   rdfs:comment "Interface Subjects are Subjects that are not linked to a behavior. In contrast, they may refer to FullySpecifiedSubjects that are described in other process models."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#JSONDataTypeDefinition
standard-pass-ont:JSONDataTypeDefinition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                         rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:CustomOrExternalDataTypeDefinition .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#KeyValuePair
standard-pass-ont:KeyValuePair rdf:type owl:Class ;
                               rdfs:subClassOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                 owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasKey ;
                                                 owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                 owl:onDataRange xsd:string
                                               ] ,
                                               [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                 owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasValue ;
                                                 owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                 owl:onDataRange xsd:string
                                               ] .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#MacroBehavior
standard-pass-ont:MacroBehavior rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:SubjectBehavior ,
                                                [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                  owl:complementOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                     owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:contains ;
                                                                     owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:EndState
                                                                   ]
                                                ] ,
                                                [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                  owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:contains ;
                                                  owl:minQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                  owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:GenericReturnToOriginReference
                                                ] ,
                                                [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                  owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:contains ;
                                                  owl:minQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                  owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:StateReference
                                                ] ;
                                owl:disjointWith standard-pass-ont:SubjectBaseBehavior ;
                                rdfs:comment """A macro behavior is a specialized behavior that may be entered and exited from a function state in another behavior.
"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#MacroState
standard-pass-ont:MacroState rdf:type owl:Class ;
                             rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:State ,
                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                               owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:referencesMacroBehavior ;
                                               owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                               owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:MacroBehavior
                                             ] ;
                             rdfs:comment "A state that references a macro behavior that is executed upon entering this state. Only after executing the macro behavior this state is finished also."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#MandatoryToEndChoiceSegmentPath
standard-pass-ont:MandatoryToEndChoiceSegmentPath rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                  owl:equivalentClass [ owl:intersectionOf ( standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegmentPath
                                                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                                               owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:isOptionalToStartChoiceSegmentPath ;
                                                                                               owl:hasValue "true"^^xsd:boolean
                                                                                             ]
                                                                                           ) ;
                                                                        rdf:type owl:Class
                                                                      ] ;
                                                  rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegmentPath .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#MandatoryToStartChoiceSegmentPath
standard-pass-ont:MandatoryToStartChoiceSegmentPath rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                    owl:equivalentClass [ owl:intersectionOf ( standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegmentPath
                                                                                               [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                                                 owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:isOptionalToEndChoiceSegmentPath ;
                                                                                                 owl:hasValue "true"^^xsd:boolean
                                                                                               ]
                                                                                             ) ;
                                                                          rdf:type owl:Class
                                                                        ] ;
                                                    rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegmentPath .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#MessageExchange
standard-pass-ont:MessageExchange rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                  rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:InteractionDescribingComponent ,
                                                  standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSElement ,
                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                    owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasMessageType ;
                                                    owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                    owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:MessageSpecification
                                                  ] ,
                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                    owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasReceiver ;
                                                    owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                    owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:Subject
                                                  ] ,
                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                    owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasSender ;
                                                    owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                    owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:Subject
                                                  ] ;
                                  rdfs:comment """A message exchange is an element in the interaction description section that specifies exactly one possibility of exchanging messages in the given process context of the model.

A message exchange is a triple of, a sender, a receiver, and the specification of the message that may be exchanged.

While message exchanges are singular occurrences, they may be grouped in MessageExchangeLists"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#MessageExchangeCondition
standard-pass-ont:MessageExchangeCondition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                           rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSElement ,
                                                           standard-pass-ont:TransitionCondition ,
                                                           [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                             owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:requiresPerformedMessageExchange ;
                                                             owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                             owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:MessageExchange
                                                           ] ;
                                           rdfs:comment "MessageExchangeConditon is the super class for Send End Receive Transition Conditions the both require either the sending or receiving (exchange) of a message to be fulfilled."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#MessageExchangeList
standard-pass-ont:MessageExchangeList rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                      rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:InteractionDescribingComponent ,
                                                      standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSElement ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:contains ;
                                                        owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:MessageExchange
                                                      ] ;
                                      rdfs:comment """While MessageExchanges are singular occurrences, they may be grouped in MessageExchangeLists. 

In graphical PASS modeling that is usually the case when one arrow between two subjects contains more than one message and thereby specifies more than one possible message exchange channel between the two subjects."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#MessageSenderTypeConstraint
standard-pass-ont:MessageSenderTypeConstraint rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:InputPoolConstraint ,
                                                              [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:references ;
                                                                owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                                owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:MessageSpecification
                                                              ] ,
                                                              [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:references ;
                                                                owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                                owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:Subject
                                                              ] ;
                                              rdfs:comment """An InputPool constraint that limits the number of message of a certain type and from a certain sender in the input pool.

E.g. \"Only one order from the same customer\" (during happy hour at the bar)"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#MessageSpecification
standard-pass-ont:MessageSpecification rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                       rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:InteractionDescribingComponent ,
                                                       standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSElement ,
                                                       [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                         owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:containsPayloadDescription ;
                                                         owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                         owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:PayloadDescription
                                                       ] ;
                                       rdfs:comment """MessageSpecification are model elements that specify the existence of a message. At minimum its name and id. 

It may contain additional specification for its payload (contained Data, exact form etc.)"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#MessageTypeConstraint
standard-pass-ont:MessageTypeConstraint rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:InputPoolConstraint ,
                                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                          owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:references ;
                                                          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                          owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:MessageSpecification
                                                        ] ;
                                        rdfs:comment """An InputPool constraint that limits the number of message of a certain type in the input pool.

E.g. You can accept only \"three request at once\""""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#ModelBuiltInDataTypes
standard-pass-ont:ModelBuiltInDataTypes rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:DataTypeDefinition ,
                                                        standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSElement .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#MultiSubject
standard-pass-ont:MultiSubject rdf:type owl:Class ;
                               owl:equivalentClass [ owl:intersectionOf ( standard-pass-ont:Subject
                                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasMaximumSubjectInstanceRestriction ;
                                                                            owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                                            owl:onDataRange [ rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                                                                                              owl:onDatatype xsd:integer ;
                                                                                              owl:withRestrictions ( [ xsd:minInclusive 2
                                                                                                                     ]
                                                                                                                   )
                                                                                            ]
                                                                          ]
                                                                        ) ;
                                                     rdf:type owl:Class
                                                   ] ;
                               rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:Subject ;
                               owl:disjointWith standard-pass-ont:SingleSubject ;
                               rdfs:comment "The Multi-Subject is term for a subject that \"has a maximum subject instantiation restriction\"  within a process context larger than 1."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#OWLDataTypeDefinition
standard-pass-ont:OWLDataTypeDefinition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:CustomOrExternalDataTypeDefinition .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#OptionalToEndChoiceSegmentPath
standard-pass-ont:OptionalToEndChoiceSegmentPath rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                 owl:equivalentClass [ owl:intersectionOf ( standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegmentPath
                                                                                            [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                                              owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:isOptionalToStartChoiceSegmentPath ;
                                                                                              owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean
                                                                                            ]
                                                                                          ) ;
                                                                       rdf:type owl:Class
                                                                     ] ;
                                                 rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegmentPath .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#OptionalToStartChoiceSegmentPath
standard-pass-ont:OptionalToStartChoiceSegmentPath rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                   owl:equivalentClass [ owl:intersectionOf ( standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegmentPath
                                                                                              [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                                                owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:isOptionalToEndChoiceSegmentPath ;
                                                                                                owl:hasValue "false"^^xsd:boolean
                                                                                              ]
                                                                                            ) ;
                                                                         rdf:type owl:Class
                                                                       ] ;
                                                   rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:ChoiceSegmentPath ;
                                                   rdfs:comment """ChoiceSegmentPath
 and (isOptionalToEndChoiceSegmentPath value false)""" .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#PASSProcessModel
standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModel rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                   rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModelElement ,
                                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                     owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                                     owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:MessageExchange
                                                   ] ,
                                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                     owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasRelationToModelComponent ;
                                                     owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:Subject
                                                   ] ,
                                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                     owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasStartSubject ;
                                                     owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:StartSubject
                                                   ] ;
                                   rdfs:comment "The main class that contains all relevant process elements"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#PASSProcessModelElement
standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModelElement rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          rdfs:subClassOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasAdditionalAttribute ;
                                                            owl:minQualifiedCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                            owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:AdditionalAttribute
                                                          ] ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasModelComponentLabel ;
                                                            owl:minQualifiedCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                            owl:onDataRange xsd:string
                                                          ] ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasModelComponentID ;
                                                            owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                            owl:onDataRange xsd:string
                                                          ] ;
                                          rdfs:comment "All sub-class/instances of subclasses of a PASS-ProcessModelElement can be considered elements of PASS Process Models"@en ,
                                                       "Every element/sub-class of SimplePASSElement is also a child of PASSProcessModelElement. This is simply a surrogate class to group all simple elements together and differ them from StandardPASS" .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#PayloadDataObjectDefinition
standard-pass-ont:PayloadDataObjectDefinition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:PayloadDescription ,
                                                              standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSElement ,
                                                              [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:contains ;
                                                                owl:minQualifiedCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                                owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:DataElementDefinition
                                                              ] ;
                                              rdfs:comment """Messages may have a description regarding their payload (what is transported with them). 

This can either be a description of a physical (real) object or a description of a (digital) data object"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#PayloadDescription
standard-pass-ont:PayloadDescription rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                     rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:DataDescribingComponent ;
                                     rdfs:comment """Messages may have a description regarding their payload (what is transported with them). 

This can either be a description of a physical (real) object or a description of a (digital) data object"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#PayloadPhysicalObjectDescription
standard-pass-ont:PayloadPhysicalObjectDescription rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                   rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:PayloadDescription ;
                                                   rdfs:comment """Messages may have a description regarding their payload (what is transported with them). 

This can either be a description of a physical (real) object or a description of a (digital) data object"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#ReceiveFunction
standard-pass-ont:ReceiveFunction rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                  rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:CommunicationAct ;
                                  owl:disjointWith standard-pass-ont:SendFunction ;
                                  rdfs:comment """Specifications/descriptions for Receive-Functions describe in detail what the subject carrier is supposed to do in a state.

DefaultFunctionReceive1_EnvoironmentChoice : present the surrounding execution environment with the given exit choices/conditions currently available depending on the current state of the subjects in-box. Waiting and not executing the receive action is an option.

DefaultFunctionReceive2_AutoReceiveEarliest: automatically execute the according activity with the highest priority as soon as possible. In contrast to DefaultFunctionReceive1, it is not an option to prolong the reception and wait e.g. for another message.

"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#ReceiveState
standard-pass-ont:ReceiveState rdf:type owl:Class ;
                               rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:StandardPASSState ,
                                               [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                 owl:complementOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                    owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasOutgoingTransition ;
                                                                    owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:DoTransition
                                                                  ]
                                               ] ,
                                               [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                 owl:complementOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                    owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasOutgoingTransition ;
                                                                    owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:SendTransition
                                                                  ]
                                               ] ,
                                               [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                 owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasFunctionSpecification ;
                                                 owl:allValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:ReceiveFunction
                                               ] ,
                                               [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                 owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasOutgoingTransition ;
                                                 owl:minQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                 owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:Transition
                                               ] ;
                               owl:disjointWith standard-pass-ont:SendState ;
                               rdfs:comment "The standard state in a PASS subject behavior diagram denoting an receive action or rather the waiting for a receive possibility."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#ReceiveTransition
standard-pass-ont:ReceiveTransition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                    rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:CommunicationTransition ,
                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                      owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasDataMappingFunction ;
                                                      owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:DataMappingIncomingToLocal
                                                    ] ,
                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                      owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasTransitionCondition ;
                                                      owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                      owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:ReceiveTransitionCondition
                                                    ] ,
                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                      owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasPriorityNumber ;
                                                      owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                      owl:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                    ] ;
                                    owl:disjointWith standard-pass-ont:SendTransition .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#ReceiveTransitionCondition
standard-pass-ont:ReceiveTransitionCondition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                             rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:MessageExchangeCondition ,
                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasReceiveType ;
                                                               owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                               owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:ReceiveType
                                                             ] ,
                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:requiresMessageSentFrom ;
                                                               owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                               owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:Subject
                                                             ] ,
                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:requiresReceptionOfMessage ;
                                                               owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                               owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:MessageSpecification
                                                             ] ,
                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasMultiReceiveLowerBound ;
                                                               owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                               owl:onDataRange xsd:positiveInteger
                                                             ] ,
                                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                               owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasMultiReceiveUpperBound ;
                                                               owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                               owl:onDataRange xsd:positiveInteger
                                                             ] ;
                                             owl:disjointWith standard-pass-ont:SendTransitionCondition ;
                                             rdfs:comment """ReceiveTransitionConditions are conditions that state that a certain message must have been taken out of a subjects in-box to be fulfilled.

These are the typical conditions defined by Receive Transitions."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#ReceiveType
standard-pass-ont:ReceiveType rdf:type owl:Class ;
                              rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:BehaviorDescribingComponent .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#ReminderEventTransitionCondition
standard-pass-ont:ReminderEventTransitionCondition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                   rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:TimeTransitionCondition ;
                                                   owl:disjointWith standard-pass-ont:TimerTransitionCondition ;
                                                   rdfs:comment """An transition (exit) condition that becomes true if a certain time since a previous trigger was set has passed.

The condition  may be defined as frequency over a given interval. --> e.g. 12x a year"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#ReminderTransition
standard-pass-ont:ReminderTransition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                     rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:TimeTransition ,
                                                     [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                       owl:complementOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                          owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasSourceState ;
                                                                          owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:SendState
                                                                        ]
                                                     ] ;
                                     owl:disjointWith standard-pass-ont:TimerTransition ;
                                     rdfs:comment "Reminder transitions are transitions that can be traversed if a certain time based event or frequency has been reached. E.g. a number of months since the last traversal of this transition or the event of a certain preset calendar date etc."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#SendFunction
standard-pass-ont:SendFunction rdf:type owl:Class ;
                               rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:CommunicationAct .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#SendState
standard-pass-ont:SendState rdf:type owl:Class ;
                            rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:StandardPASSState ,
                                            [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              owl:complementOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                 owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasOutgoingTransition ;
                                                                 owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:DoTransition
                                                               ]
                                            ] ,
                                            [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              owl:complementOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                 owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasOutgoingTransition ;
                                                                 owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:ReceiveTransition
                                                               ]
                                            ] ,
                                            [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                              owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasFunctionSpecification ;
                                              owl:allValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:SendFunction
                                            ] ,
                                            [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                              owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasOutgoingTransition ;
                                              owl:minQualifiedCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                              owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:SendingFailedTransition
                                            ] ,
                                            [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                              owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasOutgoingTransition ;
                                              owl:minQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                              owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:Transition
                                            ] ,
                                            [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                              owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasOutgoingTransition ;
                                              owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                              owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:SendTransition
                                            ] ;
                            rdfs:comment "The standard state in a PASS subject behavior diagram denoting a send action"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#SendTransition
standard-pass-ont:SendTransition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                 rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:CommunicationTransition ,
                                                 [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                   owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasDataMappingFunction ;
                                                   owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:DataMappingLocalToOutgoing
                                                 ] ,
                                                 [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                   owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasTransitionCondition ;
                                                   owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                   owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:SendTransitionCondition
                                                 ] .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#SendTransitionCondition
standard-pass-ont:SendTransitionCondition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:MessageExchangeCondition ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasSendType ;
                                                            owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                            owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:SendType
                                                          ] ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:requiresMessageSentTo ;
                                                            owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                            owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:Subject
                                                          ] ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:requiresSendingOfMessage ;
                                                            owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                            owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:MessageSpecification
                                                          ] ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasMultiSendLowerBound ;
                                                            owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                            owl:onDataRange xsd:positiveInteger
                                                          ] ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasMultiSendUpperBound ;
                                                            owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                            owl:onDataRange xsd:positiveInteger
                                                          ] ;
                                          rdfs:comment """SendTransitionConditions are conditions that state that a certain message must have been successfully passed to another subjects in-box to be fulfilled.

These are the typical conditions defined by Send transitions."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#SendType
standard-pass-ont:SendType rdf:type owl:Class ;
                           rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:BehaviorDescribingComponent .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#SenderTypeConstraint
standard-pass-ont:SenderTypeConstraint rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                       rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:InputPoolConstraint ,
                                                       [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                         owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:references ;
                                                         owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                         owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:Subject
                                                       ] ;
                                       rdfs:comment """An InputPool constraint that limits the number of message  from a certain Sender subject in the input pool.

E.g. as long as a customer has non non-fulfilled request of any type he may not place messages"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#SendingFailedCondition
standard-pass-ont:SendingFailedCondition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                         rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:TransitionCondition .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#SendingFailedTransition
standard-pass-ont:SendingFailedTransition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:Transition ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasSourceState ;
                                                            owl:allValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:SendState
                                                          ] ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasTransitionCondition ;
                                                            owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                            owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:SendingFailedCondition
                                                          ] ;
                                          rdfs:comment "Concept: if during execution the sending of a message fails after a certain condition this transition specifies a default alternative"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#SimplePASSElement
standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSElement rdf:type owl:Class .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#SingleSubject
standard-pass-ont:SingleSubject rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                owl:equivalentClass [ owl:intersectionOf ( standard-pass-ont:Subject
                                                                           [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                             owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasMaximumSubjectInstanceRestriction ;
                                                                             owl:hasValue 1
                                                                           ]
                                                                         ) ;
                                                      rdf:type owl:Class
                                                    ] ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:Subject ;
                                rdfs:comment "Single Subject are subject with a maximumInstanceRestriction of 1"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#StandardPASSState
standard-pass-ont:StandardPASSState rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                    rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSElement ,
                                                    standard-pass-ont:State ;
                                    rdfs:comment "A super class to the standard PASS states: Do, Receive and Send"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#StartSubject
standard-pass-ont:StartSubject rdf:type owl:Class ;
                               rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:Subject ;
                               rdfs:comment """Subjects that start their behavior with a Do or Send state are active in a process context from the beginning instead of requiring a message from another subject.

Usually there should be only one Start subject in a process context."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#State
standard-pass-ont:State rdf:type owl:Class ;
                        rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:BehaviorDescribingComponent ,
                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                          owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:guardedBy ;
                                          owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:GuardBehavior
                                        ] ,
                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                          owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasIncomingTransition ;
                                          owl:minQualifiedCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                          owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:Transition
                                        ] ,
                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                          owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasOutgoingTransition ;
                                          owl:minQualifiedCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                          owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:Transition
                                        ] ,
                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                          owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:belongsTo ;
                                          owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                          owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:Action
                                        ] ,
                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                          owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasFunctionSpecification ;
                                          owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                          owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:FunctionSpecification
                                        ] ;
                        rdfs:comment "A state in the behavior descriptions of a model"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#StateReference
standard-pass-ont:StateReference rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                 rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:State ,
                                                 [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                   owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:references ;
                                                   owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                   owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:State
                                                 ] ;
                                 rdfs:comment "A state reference is a model component that is a reference to a state in another behavior. For most modeling aspects it is a normal state." .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#StaticSubjectExecutionMapping
standard-pass-ont:StaticSubjectExecutionMapping rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:SubjectExecutionMapping ;
                                                rdfs:comment "A mapping between subjects and agents can be done simple and direct (or \"static\"). Here, agents are directly mapped to subjects and therefore eligible to execute them. The only information necessary to know about the execution system is the existence of the agents in order to assign subjects to them."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#Subject
standard-pass-ont:Subject rdf:type owl:Class ;
                          rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:InteractionDescribingComponent ,
                                          standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSElement ,
                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasIncomingMessageExchange ;
                                            owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:MessageExchange
                                          ] ,
                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasOutgoingMessageExchange ;
                                            owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:MessageExchange
                                          ] ,
                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasSubjectExecutionMapping ;
                                            owl:minQualifiedCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                            owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:SubjectExecutionMapping
                                          ] ,
                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasMaximumSubjectInstanceRestriction ;
                                            owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                            owl:onDataRange xsd:int
                                          ] ;
                          rdfs:comment "The subject is the core model element of a subject-oriented PASS process model."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#SubjectBaseBehavior
standard-pass-ont:SubjectBaseBehavior rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                      rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:SimplePASSElement ,
                                                      standard-pass-ont:SubjectBehavior ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        owl:complementOf [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                           owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:contains ;
                                                                           owl:someValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:StateReference
                                                                         ]
                                                      ] ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasEndState ;
                                                        owl:minQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                        owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:EndState
                                                      ] ;
                                      rdfs:comment "The standard behavior model type"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#SubjectBehavior
standard-pass-ont:SubjectBehavior rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                  rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:PASSProcessModelElement ,
                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                    owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:contains ;
                                                    owl:allValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:BehaviorDescribingComponent
                                                  ] ,
                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                    owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasInitialState ;
                                                    owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                    owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:InitialStateOfBehavior
                                                  ] ,
                                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                    owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasPriorityNumber ;
                                                    owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                    owl:onDataRange xsd:nonNegativeInteger
                                                  ] ;
                                  rdfs:comment """Additional to the subject interaction a PASS Model consist of multiple descriptions of subject's behaviors. These are graphs described with the means of $BehaviorDescribingComponents$

A subject in a model may be linked to more than one behavior."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#SubjectDataDefinition
standard-pass-ont:SubjectDataDefinition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                        rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:DataDescribingComponent ,
                                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                          owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:contains ;
                                                          owl:minQualifiedCardinality "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                          owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:DataElementDefinition
                                                        ] ;
                                        rdfs:comment """Subjects may have a description regarding their individual data store or their individual data base (subject data) 

This could  be a description of a physical (real) object but for BOs a a description of a (digital) data object"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#SubjectExecutionMapping
standard-pass-ont:SubjectExecutionMapping rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:InteractionDescribingComponent ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasExecutionMappingDefinition ;
                                                            owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                            owl:onDataRange xsd:string
                                                          ] ;
                                          rdfs:comment """On an \"atomic\" level any socio-technical system consist of various \"types of agents\", individual human beings, physical machines that are meant for single tasks (e.g. production machines for stamping), and IT components that are used to coordinated them.

When implementing a subject-oriented process model, it is necessary to state which \"agent\" is responsible for the execution of which subject. This concept is called mapping; as verb \"to map\" subjects to agents, or as noun to create \"a mapping\" between subjects and agents.

To be useful, these mappings must be written in a form that can be understood by the execution system in order to assign the correct agents to be subject-carriers for the correct subjects. The mapping is used to answer question like: \"Is an agents allowed to execute a subject?\", \"What resources/agents are available to execute a subject?\"."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#TimeBasedReminderTransition
standard-pass-ont:TimeBasedReminderTransition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:ReminderTransition .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#TimeBasedReminderTransitionCondition
standard-pass-ont:TimeBasedReminderTransitionCondition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                       rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:ReminderEventTransitionCondition ;
                                                       rdfs:comment "e.g. the reoccurrence of a a time based frequency (\"every 10 minuets\",  \"4 times an hour\")"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#TimeTransition
standard-pass-ont:TimeTransition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                 rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:Transition ;
                                 rdfs:comment """Generic super calls for all TimeTransitions, transitions with conditions based on time events. E.g.passing of a certain time duration or the (reoccurring) calendar event.		
		"""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#TimeTransitionCondition
standard-pass-ont:TimeTransitionCondition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:TransitionCondition ,
                                                          [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                            owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasTimeValue ;
                                                            owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                            owl:onDataRange xsd:string
                                                          ] ;
                                          rdfs:comment "A condition that is deemed 'true' and thus the according edge is gone, if: a surrounding execution system has deemed the time since entering the state and starting with the execution of the according action as too long (predefined by the outgoing edge)"@en ,
                                                       "A condition that is true if a certain time defined has passed since the state this condition is attached to via its transition has been entered. (This is the standard TimeOut condition)"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#TimerTransition
standard-pass-ont:TimerTransition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                  rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:TimeTransition ;
                                  rdfs:comment "Timer transitions, denote time outs for the state they originate from.  The condition for a timer transition is that a certain amount of time has passed since the state it originates from has been entered."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#TimerTransitionCondition
standard-pass-ont:TimerTransitionCondition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                           rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:TimeTransitionCondition .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#Transition
standard-pass-ont:Transition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                             rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:BehaviorDescribingComponent ,
                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                               owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasSourceState ;
                                               owl:allValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:State
                                             ] ,
                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                               owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasTargetState ;
                                               owl:allValuesFrom standard-pass-ont:State
                                             ] ,
                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                               owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasTransitionCondition ;
                                               owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                               owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:TransitionCondition
                                             ] ,
                                             [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                               owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:belongsTo ;
                                               owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                               owl:onClass standard-pass-ont:Action
                                             ] ;
                             rdfs:comment "An edge defines the transition between two states. A transition can be traversed if the outcome of the action of the state it originates from satisfies a certain condition specified by it's \"Alternative\". In the model these conditions are defined for and attached to the transition --> Transition Condition (when a transition originates from a state, its transition condition defines one of possibly multipe exit conditions for that state. "@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#TransitionCondition
standard-pass-ont:TransitionCondition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                      rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:BehaviorDescribingComponent ,
                                                      [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                        owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasToolSpecificDefinition ;
                                                        owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                        owl:onDataRange xsd:string
                                                      ] ;
                                      rdfs:comment """An Transition condition defines an alternatives for a state that the transition the condition is attached to, originates from. An alternative (to leave the state) is only a real alternative if the condition is fulfilled (technically: if that according function returns \"true\")

Note: Technically and during execution \"conditions\" belong to states. They define when it is allowed to leave that state. However, in PASS models exit conditions for states are defined and connected to the according transition edges. Therefore transition conditions are individual entities and not DataProperties.

The according matching must be done by the model execution environment.

By its existence, an edge/transition defines one possible follow up \"state\" for its state of origin. It is coupled with an \"Exit Condition\" for that state (the transition condition) that must be fulfilled in the originating state in order to leave the state."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#UserCancelTransition
standard-pass-ont:UserCancelTransition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                       rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:Transition ;
                                       rdfs:comment """A user cancel transition denotes the possibility to exit a receive state without the reception of a specific message. 

The user cancel allows for an arbitrary decision by a subject carrier/processor to abort a waiting process."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#XSD-DataTypeDefinition
standard-pass-ont:XSD-DataTypeDefinition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                         rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:CustomOrExternalDataTypeDefinition ;
                                         rdfs:comment "XML Schemata Description (XSD) is an established technology for describing structure of Data Objects (XML documents) with many tools available that can verify a document against the standard definition" .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#YearMonthTimerTransition
standard-pass-ont:YearMonthTimerTransition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                           rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:TimerTransition ;
                                           rdfs:comment """Timer transitions, denote time outs for the state they originate from.  The condition for a timer transition is that a certain amount of time has passed since the state it originates from has been entered.

Year or Month timers measure time in calendar years or months. The exact definitions for years and months depends on relevant or legal  geographical location of the subject."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#YearMonthTimerTransitionCondition
standard-pass-ont:YearMonthTimerTransitionCondition rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                    rdfs:subClassOf standard-pass-ont:TimerTransitionCondition ,
                                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                      owl:onProperty standard-pass-ont:hasTimeValue ;
                                                                      owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                                      owl:onDataRange xsd:yearMonthDuration
                                                                    ] ;
                                                    rdfs:comment """A Timer Transition Condition that is fulfilled if a certain time defined in calendar years or months has passed since the state this condition belongs to has been entered.

The exact specification of year and especially month depends on a subjects legal or geographical location."""@en .


#################################################################
#    Individuals
#################################################################

###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DefaultFunctionDo1_EnvironmentChoice
standard-pass-ont:DefaultFunctionDo1_EnvironmentChoice rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                standard-pass-ont:DoFunction ;
                                                       rdfs:comment "The default doFunction 1: is to present the surrounding execution environment with the given exit choices/conditions and receive choice of one Exit Option --> define its Condition to be fulfilled in order to go to the next according state."@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DefaultFunctionDo2_AutomaticEvaluation
standard-pass-ont:DefaultFunctionDo2_AutomaticEvaluation rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                  standard-pass-ont:DoFunction ;
                                                         rdfs:comment "The default doFunction 2: execute automatic rule evaluation (see DoTransitionCondition)"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DefaultFunctionReceive1_EnvironmentChoice
standard-pass-ont:DefaultFunctionReceive1_EnvironmentChoice rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                     standard-pass-ont:ReceiveFunction ;
                                                            rdfs:comment "The default receive function is to present the surrounding execution environment with the given exit choices/conditions currently available depending on the current state of the subjects in-box. The surrounding may choose a few of its options"@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DefaultFunctionReceive2_AutoReceiveEarliest
standard-pass-ont:DefaultFunctionReceive2_AutoReceiveEarliest rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                       standard-pass-ont:ReceiveFunction ;
                                                              rdfs:comment """DefaultFunctionReceive2_AutoReceiveEarliest 

Is a function that executes the according activity with the highest priority as soon as possible.

In contrast to DefaultFunctionReceive1, it is not an option to prolong the reception and wait e.g. for another message."""@en .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#DefaultFunctionSend
standard-pass-ont:DefaultFunctionSend rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                               standard-pass-ont:SendFunction .


###  http://www.i2pm.net/standard-pass-ont#InputPoolConstraintStrategy-Blocking
standard-pass-ont:InputPoolConstraintStrategy-Blocking rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
